OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F308A1791485298
OL,3,CVerstappen navigates start chaos to
OL,4,Ctriumph in Bahrain Grand Prix
OL,6,FMercedes told Antonelli over the radio
OL,7,Fthat it appeared Russell had suffered
OL,8,Fa power unit problem.
OL,10,FAntonelli finished second, and
OL,11,FFerrari's Lewis Hamilton passed
OL,12,FVerstappen's Red Bull teammate Isack
OL,13,FHadjar for third.
OL,15,FThe first wet-weather race for F1 in
OL,16,F2026 started more than 90 minutes
OL,17,Flater than planned. The start was
OL,18,Ffirst delayed 40 minutes for heavy
OL,19,Frain, then suspended again when cars
OL,20,Fhad apparent software problems on the
OL,21,Fformation lap.
OL,1,W~s1{$~k4{$k7                    G2/5
OL,2,W,.!/  +.!/*%*%R,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,RpppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/sport
OL,24,ANext Page BNat Sport CNat Radio FRewind
FL,309,300,200,120,000,100
PN,30803
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F308A1791485298
OL,3,CVerstappen navigates start chaos to
OL,4,Ctriumph in Bahrain Grand Prix
OL,6,FSoftware problems struck Verstappen
OL,7,Fand Hamilton, connected to the
OL,8,Frequired 50-50 split between
OL,9,Fcombustion and battery power, and they
OL,10,Fcould not get their cars to operate.
OL,12,FThe grid limped back to the pit lane,
OL,13,Fand although the rain had long since
OL,14,Fstopped, a further 53 minutes passed
OL,15,Fbefore the green light was given by
OL,16,Fthe sport's chiefs to try again.
OL,1,W~s1{$~k4{$k7                    G3/5
OL,2,W,.!/  +.!/*%*%R,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
